From: Andrey Stoyan <andrey.stoyan.csam@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 22:40:18 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 04/44] =?UTF-8?q?feat(chexc):=20capability=20argument=20ch?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ecking=20=E2=80=94=20CapabilityCheck=20pass=20(M3,=20=C2=A73.3/?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=C2=A73.5)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- New CAPABILITY_CHECK compile stage between SEMA and DESUGAR_AFTER_SEMA;
  self-contained module src/Sema/CapabilityCheck/ (pure check: no type
  mutation, no escape analysis per author ruling).
- Supplies: decl clauses, try catch-pattern types (E1|E2 = two; wildcard =
  Exception; catch/finally outside, try-with-resources inside), literal
  capTys from expected type; spawn bodies get an empty scope stack.
- Demands: throw sites; call sites via instantiated callee FuncTy (generic,
  ctor, operator, function-value calls uniformly); default-parameter values
  against the callee's own scope; instance field initializers must satisfy
  every constructor's scope; static/top-level initializers have no scope.
- Miss-handler interface (report|collect) — the §6.3 inference seam.
- Flag: canonical --enable-checked-exceptions[=error|warn] (proposal name),
  alias --enable-chexc; warn mode emits warnings in new 'chexc' warn group
  (-Woff chexc works); bare flag = error.
- Diagnostics per author ruling (no @ local! pre-Modal).

Gate: scopes 7/7, parse 11/11, types 10/10; ctest 49/49; Parser/Sema LLT
3934/3934; clang-format clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
